WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.827
Here we combine variables, arithmetic, and formatting in one example.

00:00:04.827 --> 00:00:10.652
Sales are twenty-five hundred dollars and costs are seventeen hundred fifty dollars,

00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:13.852
so profit is seven hundred fifty dollars.

00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:21.176
Margin is profit divided by sales, which gives zero point three, or thirty percent when formatted.

00:00:21.776 --> 00:00:25.778
Profit and margin describe related but different ideas.

00:00:25.778 --> 00:00:27.908
Profit is a dollar amount.

00:00:27.908 --> 00:00:33.038
Margin is a ratio that tells us what share of sales remains as profit.

00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:36.673
Increase costs and run the example again.

00:00:36.673 --> 00:00:39.568
Both profit and margin should move downward.
